title: date_bellemere_4_C
location: quarters
---

You both taste the mikan chicken at the same time. It's sharp and sweet, mixed with spicy and savory. The citrus stays on your tongue a little longer than any other flavor, like the lingering tone of a plucked violin.
You serve the pie.
It's silky and sweet and perfect. In fact, better than perfect.
You must have made some sound of approval, because Bellemere says-
Bellemere: This might be the best pie I've ever had! The crust... wow! It's like... like a wedding cake, somehow? What did you put in it?
{$name}: Uh, might be the almond paste? I mean, of course it turned out great! Did you doubt me?
She laughs.
Bellemere: Never.
Bellemere looks very happy in that moment, more content and mellow than usual.
Her hair is an auburn that looks nearly purple in the starlight. You would normally use a myriad of adjectives to describe the woman: strong, belligerent, funny, entertaining... but beautiful is one that strikes you every once in a while with a gravity so strong  it's shocking. Yes, this kick-ass Marine is beautiful.
She notices you staring.
Bellemere: What?
{$name}: Uh... nothing.
You blush, and Bellemere looks pleased to have flustered you so thoroughly (even if she doesn't understand fully why).
The night ends and you return to your own apartment, stomach full of good food and mind full of peaceful memories.
<<set $bd4_points += 2>>
<<jump date_bellemere_4_DateEndNice>>
===

title: date_bellemere_4_mint
location: quarters
---

You hurry to grab the mint from the shelves, pay for the groceries, and make your way back to Bellemere's apartment.
Bellemere: Hey, you're back!
Bellemere has beaten you back to her apartment. She even has the oven preheated and is mixing something in a bowl, already! So fast!
{$name}: Is this a race?
Bellemere: No, I'm just fast!
She laughs.
Bellemere: Did you get what you needed?
{$name}: Er.... hopefully?
Bellemere: Oh, that sounds promising.
{$name}: I mean, yeah, I got everything on the list, but I may have improvised one item... I lost my list. Pretty sure we're good!
Bellemere seems on the incredulous side, but nods towards some supplies set on her small counter for you. Time to get to work!
You measure your flour carefully and then start mixing your dough for the pie crust. This is the point where it could all go right or very wrong, right at the start, so you double check your recipe...
Whoops! Mint was not the correct missing ingredient! Well... you're pretty sure it'll work though, right?
You mix all of your spices in with the batter and start rolling the dough out, laying it nearly over the provided pie-tin. You even dimple the edges artistically, proud of your work. The filling takes a while, but when you put it in the oven it smells amazing as it bakes. The whole apartment is filled with the sweet scent.
You open the patio door to release some of the heat from the stove, the cool ocean breeze adding to the cozy atmosphere.
{$name}: Hey, you have a table out here. Want to eat on the balcony?
Bellemere: It's a nice night- why not? You set the table while this pie bakes and I finish up the chicken.
You manage to find some plates and silverware inside a cupboard... and note a few candles set on the opposite side. Should you...?
-> Yes, use the candles to set the mood!
    <<jump date_bellemere_4_candles_3>>
-> No, keep it simple.
    <<jump date_bellemere_4_simple_3>>
===

title: date_bellemere_4_simple_3
location: quarters
---

You set the table, the light from inside the apartment filtering out through the glass door to illuminate the space. Maybe it's a bit less romantic, this way, but...
Romantic? Is that what you're doing, here? You certainly like Bellemere a lot, but you're not sure how she feels about you.
You help Bellemere bring out the food and the two of you sit down across from each other. You hope your dish turns out well; you'd like to impress her.
<<jump date_bellemere_4_D>>
===

title: date_bellemere_4_candles_3
location: quarters
---

You grab the candles, using them to decorate as you set the table.
When Bellemere finally finishes the chicken and your pie comes out of the oven to cool, the redhead joins you out on the balcony. She looks on with approving eyes, setting the bowl of food down between the lovingly-set plates.
It's nothing fancy; the space is small, the deck simple finished wood. However... you managed to make it look very nice, placing candles along the balustrade and on the table. The sun has set, and the stars provide a gorgeous backdrop to the black ocean beyond the edge of the small town.
Bellemere: Beautiful.
{$name}: Me, the food, or the view?
Bellemere: Ha! Cheesy! All of the above, I suppose?
<<jump date_bellemere_4_D>>
===

title: date_bellemere_4_D
location: quarters
---

You both taste the mikan chicken at the same time. It's sharp and sweet, mixed with spicy and savory. The citrus stays on your tongue a little longer than any other flavor, like the lingering tone of a plucked violin.
You serve the pie.
It's...
Uh...
You spit it out back onto your plate in a messy pile. Gross.
Bellemere: Oh, god... what have you done!?
{$name}: I don't know!
Bellemere: It's like... like toothpaste and orange juice!
{$name}: I know, I tasted it too!
You can't even defend yourself. It was vile. Horrific. Probably the worst thing you've ever made.
Bellemere: Well... at least this will be funny tomorrow... when I don't want to vomit.
{$name}: I'm sorry...
Bellemere: Nah, I just learned an important lesson: don't trust you with cooking!
You feel bad, but Bellemere seems to be handling it with humor as you part ways, and you return to your apartment in gastrinal distress.
<<set $bd4_points += 1>>
<<jump date_bellemere_4_DateEndOops>> (+1)
===

